s physical activity include any bodily movement that burns calories, such as walking and strength training, which are particularly beneficial for elderly individuals. Overall, physical activity is recognized as one of the four pillars of comprehensive treatment for frailty in the elderly, highlighting its importance in promoting a healthy lifestyle and managing health conditions effectively.", "ALIMENTACIÓN DIGNA:La alimentación digna se refiere a la provisión de una nutrición adecuada y respetuosa para ancianos dependientes.", "DENSIDAD MINERAL ÓSEA:\"DENSIDAD MINERAL ÓSEA\" refers to bone mineral density (DMO), a crucial measure used to assess bone strength and predict fracture risk, particularly in patients with osteoporosis. It is an important factor in evaluating the risk of osteoporosis and fractures in older adults. Additionally, DMO is often assessed in patients with Anorexia Nervosa to evaluate their bone health. The term also encompasses the amount of mineral matter per square centimeter of bones, which can be influenced by nutritional interventions in various patient populations, including those with respiratory diseases and celiac disease. Furthermore, DMO can improve in children with glycogen storage diseases when dietary recommendations are adhered to. Overall, \"densidad mineral ósea\" serves as an indicator of bone health, with adequate nutrition playing a significant role in enhancing bone density, especially in geriatric patients.", "MÉTODOS DE ADMINISTRACIÓN:Los métodos de administración se refieren a las técnicas utilizadas para proporcionar nutrición enteral a los pacientes, que pueden ser continuos o intermitentes.", "FÓRMULAS ENTERALES:", "ENFERMOS GERIÁTRICOS:Los enfermos geriátricos son pacientes de edad avanzada que requieren atención médica especializada debido a múltiples condiciones de salud y a menudo enfrentan problemas de nutrición.", "CUIDADOS PALIATIVOS ONCOLÓGICOS:Son cuidados paliativos específicos para pacientes con cáncer incurable, enfocados en el control de síntomas asociados al tumor o a su tratamiento.", "CUIDADOS PALIATIVOS NO ONCOLÓGICOS:Son cuidados paliativos dirigidos a pacientes con enfermedades crónicas avanzadas y procesos degenerativos en fase terminal.", "GÓMEZ CANDELA C:Gómez Candela C is a prominent researcher associated with the NADYA group, where they focus on studies related to home parenteral nutrition and home enteral nutrition in Spain. In addition to their research contributions, Gómez Candela C has authored significant works, including a chapter on nutrition in eating disorders for a medical textbook and guidelines on home artificial nutrition specifically for oncological patients. They have also emphasized the importance of maintaining a balanced omega 6/omega 3 ratio for overall health. Furthermore, Gómez Candela C serves as an editor for the \"Manual de recomendaciones nutricionales en pacientes geriátricos,\" where they contribute to the development of nutritional recommendations for geriatric patients.", "COS BLANCO AI:Cos Blanco AI is an author of a chapter in the Manual de recomendaciones nutricionales en pacientes geriátricos, focusing on artificial nutrition.", "SALGADO ALBA A:Salgado Alba A is an author of a chapter in the Manual de geriatría, discussing comprehensive geriatric assessment.", "TENA DÁVILA MC:Tena Dávila MC is an author of a chapter in the Manual de geriatría, addressing malnutrition in the elderly.", "VALERO ZANUY MA:Valero Zanuy MA is an author of a chapter in the Manual de recomendaciones nutricionales en pacientes geriátricos, discussing malnutrition in the elderly.", "WANDEN-BERGHE LOZANO C:Wanden-Berghe Lozano C is an author of a chapter in the Intervención nutricional en el anciano, focusing on nutritional requirements in the elderly.", "CASTRO LOZANO MA:", "ASTENIA:Astenia is a condition characterized by a state of physical weakness or lack of energy. It is commonly recognized as a symptom associated with advanced cancer, where it is highly prevalent among non-oncological palliative patients. Additionally, astenia can also manifest as a symptom in individuals with celiac disease, further highlighting its association with various health conditions."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}